  {
   "id": "moed_katan.13b.3",
   "daf": "13b",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ מְחַפִּין אֶת הַקְּצִיעוֹת בְּקַשׁ. רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: אַף מְעַבִּין. מוֹכְרֵי פֵירוֹת, כְּסוּת וְכֵלִים — מוֹכְרִים בְּצִנְעָה לְצוֹרֶךְ הַמּוֹעֵד. הַצַּיָּידִין וְהַדָּשׁוֹשׁוֹת וְהַגָּרוֹסוֹת — עוֹשִׂין בְּצִנְעָה לְצוֹרֶךְ הַמּוֹעֵד. רַבִּי יוֹסֵי אוֹמֵר: הֵם הֶחֱמִירוּ עַל עַצְמָן.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» On the intermediate days of a Festival, «figs» that were spread out to dry «may be covered with straw» to protect them from rain and dew. «Rabbi Yehuda says: One may even condense» the figs. «Those who sell produce, clothing, and utensils may sell» them «in private, for the sake of the Festival. Fishermen, and groats makers [dashoshot], and» bean «pounders,» who pulverize the beans, «may ply» their trades «in private for the sake of the Festival. Rabbi Yosei says: They were stringent with themselves» to refrain from this work even with respect to what was needed for the Festival."
  }
 ],
